					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465243#post-1433369</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465243/scp-616-j#post-1433369</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 30 Apr 2012 20:44:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Bland</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>663362</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Upvoted with the following observations:</p> <ul> <li>&quot;SCP-616 may only be performed by&#8230;&quot; except SCP-616 is the <em>book</em> not the ritural. &quot;SCP-616 may only be <em>accessed</em> by&#8230;&quot;</li> <li>&quot;SCP-616 was created in response to a directive by the SCP Foundation Ethics Committee in response to increasing demand for Class D personnel for testing purposes that threatened to exceed the number that could be safely inducted from standard channels.&quot; &#8230;in response to&#8230;in response to&#8230; It's kind of awkward, but I don't have better phrasing at the moment.</li> </ul> <p>That said, I like it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
